WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.008 --> 00:00:08.873
Kayla groaned as she joined Kobe and Jenny at a table.

2
00:00:08.874 --> 00:00:14.042
"I hate science experiments."

3
00:00:14.043 --> 00:00:17.867
"Science experiments are fun," Jenny said.

4
00:00:17.868 --> 00:00:21.101
"We just need a good idea."

5
00:00:21.102 --> 00:00:29.193
Kayla sighed. "I'm sick of making volcanoes explode."

6
00:00:29.194 --> 00:00:32.207
"We could grow mold," Kobe said.

7
00:00:32.208 --> 00:00:37.334
Jenny made a face. "Mold is gross."

8
00:00:37.335 --> 00:00:39.745
Kayla looked bored.

9
00:00:39.746 --> 00:00:42.654
She ripped a sheet of paper from her notebook.

10
00:00:42.655 --> 00:00:44.308
Jenny frowned.

11
00:00:44.309 --> 00:00:48.148
"Mr. Netter said we're supposed to work together, Kayla.

12
00:00:48.149 --> 00:00:52.066
You're not helping us."

13
00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:56.916
Kayla was folding wings on a paper airplane.

14
00:00:56.917 --> 00:00:59.319
"Let's test this plane."

15
00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:01.650
"Huh?" Kobe said.

16
00:01:01.651 --> 00:01:05.851
"We can measure how far it flies," Kayla said.

17
00:01:05.852 --> 00:01:08.947
"Good idea!" Kobe said.

18
00:01:08.948 --> 00:01:13.777
"It sounds scientific and fun," Jenny agreed.

19
00:01:13.778 --> 00:01:15.923
She looked at her notebook.

20
00:01:15.924 --> 00:01:22.186
"Step one of the scientific method is to ask questions."

21
00:01:22.187 --> 00:01:27.348
"How about, how does weight affect flight distance?" Kobe said.

22
00:01:27.349 --> 00:01:28.994
Everyone nodded.

23
00:01:28.995 --> 00:01:32.153
Jenny wrote down the question.

24
00:01:32.154 --> 00:01:35.973
"Next we have to come up with a hypothesis.

25
00:01:35.974 --> 00:01:39.937
That's a guess about what will happen."

26
00:01:39.938 --> 00:01:44.459
The kids did some research about airplane flight.

27
00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:50.448
"Hmm," said Kayla. "I think a lighter plane will fly farther."

28
00:01:50.449 --> 00:01:52.892
"Me too," Kobe said.

29
00:01:52.893 --> 00:01:58.221
"That's our hypothesis: a light paper plane will fly farther."

30
00:01:58.222 --> 00:02:02.314
Jenny wrote it down.

31
00:02:02.315 --> 00:02:08.788
"To test our hypothesis, we'll have to change the plane's weight."

32
00:02:08.789 --> 00:02:11.759
Kobe got some paperclips.

33
00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:14.756
"We can use these to add weight."

34
00:02:14.757 --> 00:02:20.104
Kayla grabbed her airplane. "Let's find a runway!"

35
00:02:20.105 --> 00:02:25.237
The kids went out into the hallway.

36
00:02:25.238 --> 00:02:29.495
Kayla threw the plane and Kobe measured where it stopped.

37
00:02:29.496 --> 00:02:32.055
"My turn!" said Kobe.

38
00:02:32.056 --> 00:02:37.320
"We should try to throw the plane the same way each time," said Jenny.

39
00:02:37.321 --> 00:02:42.630
"So Kayla should keep flying the plane."

40
00:02:42.631 --> 00:02:49.047
Kayla flew the plane several more times and Kobe measured each flight's distance.

41
00:02:49.048 --> 00:02:54.035
Next they added two paperclips to the plane.

42
00:02:54.036 --> 00:02:57.564
They flew and measured several more times.

43
00:02:57.565 --> 00:03:01.922
Jenny recorded the results.

44
00:03:01.923 --> 00:03:05.961
"Let's try four paperclips now," Kayla said.

45
00:03:05.962 --> 00:03:09.950
They flew the plane again.

46
00:03:09.951 --> 00:03:13.086
"Time to analyze our data!" Kobe said.

47
00:03:13.087 --> 00:03:17.470
"Uh-oh." Jenny studied the results with a frown.

48
00:03:17.471 --> 00:03:21.844
"Our plane flew farthest with two paperclips.

49
00:03:21.845 --> 00:03:24.940
Our hypothesis was incorrect."

50
00:03:24.941 --> 00:03:27.330
"That's okay," Kobe said.

51
00:03:27.331 --> 00:03:31.970
"Mr. Netter said a science experiment is for testing ideas.

52
00:03:31.971 --> 00:03:36.959
Even if your hypothesis is incorrect, you still learn stuff."

53
00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:45.586
Kayla grinned. "I learned something—science experiments can be fun!"

